\par \pard {\f5 
\par   There are 2 options for changing }{\f5\uldb Modes}{\v\f5 Modes}{\f5 .
\par 
\par 
\par   Option 1: Move the mouse cursor to the center of the knob and click either the right of left mouse button. the right mouse button rotates the knob clockwise and the left mouse button turns the knob counterclockwise.
\par 
\par   Option 2: Clicking on any of the six buttons (AM. USB, LSB, ISB, FM or CW). with the right mouse button will select that choice.
\par 
\par See Also:
\par   }{\f5\uldb Modes}{\v\f5 Modes}{\f5 
\par   }{\f5\uldb Turning Knobs}{\v\f5 Turning_Knobs}{\f5 
\par 
\par }\pard \qc {\f5 \page }{\cs16\super #{\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super #} Changing_Monitor}${\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super $} Changing Monitor}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s15 \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super K} Changing Monitor}} {\fs44 
Changing Monitor}
\par \pard {\f5 
\par   There are 2 options for changing the }{\f5\uldb Monitor}{\v\f5 Monitor}{\f5 .
\par 
\par 
\par   Option 1: Move the mouse cursor to the center of the knob and click either the right of left mouse button. the right mouse button increases the monitor and the left mouse button decreases mic gain.
\par 
\par   Option 2: Clicking the right mouse button while the mouse cursor is in the monitor window, but outside of the picture of the knob will cause the knob to turn to point the cursor. 9:00 is minimum gain, and 3:00 is maximum. The range from 3:01 to 8:59 is 
ignored.
\par 
\par See Also:
\par   }{\f5\uldb Monitor}{\v\f5 Monitor}{\f5 
\par   }{\f5\uldb Turning Knobs}{\v\f5 Turning_Knobs}{\f5 
\par 
\par }\pard \qc \page {\cs16\super #{\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super #} Changing_PTT}${\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super $} Changing PTT}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s15 \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super K} Changing PTT}} {\fs44 Changing PTT}{\fs32 

\par }\pard {\f5 
\par   There are 4 choices for changing PTT. In order to enter transmit, you must be tuned to a valid amateur frequency, & must have entered your callsign in the }{\f5\uldb Callsign}{\v\f5 Callsign}{\f5 
 window. If you have not met these conditions, you will receive a warning message, and RADWARE will stay in recieve.
\par 
\par   Option 1: Left Click on RECV or XMIT in the }{\f5\uldb PTT}{\v\f5 PTT}{\f5  window.
\par 
\par   Option 2: Right Click or left Click on the knob in the PTT window will toggle between Transmit and Receive.
\par 
\par   Option 3: Pressing the Escape key while in RADWARE will toggle the PTT.
\par 
\par   Option 4: Via an }{\f5\uldb External PTT Control}{\v\f5 External_PTT_Keyer}{\f5 .
\par 
\par See also:
\par     }{\f5\uldb Callsign}{\v\f5 Callsign}{\f5 
\par     }{\f5\uldb External PTT Control}{\v\f5 External_PTT_Keyer}{\f5 
\par     }{\f5\uldb PTT}{\v\f5 PTT}{\f5 
\par 
\par }\pard \qc \page {\cs16\super #{\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super #} Changing_RX_Antenna}${\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super $} Changing RX DC Antenna Power}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s15 \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super K}
 Changing RX DC Antenna Power}} {\fs44 Changing RX DC Antenna Power}
\par \pard {\f5 
\par   There are 2 options for changing }{\f5\uldb RX DC Antenna Power}{\v\f5 RX_Antenna}{\f5 
\par 
\par 
\par   Option 1: Move the mouse cursor to the center of the knob and click either the right of left mouse button. the right mouse button rotates the knob clockwise and the left mouse button turns the knob counterclockwise.
\par 
\par   Option 2: Clicking on either button (ON or OFF). with the right mouse button will select that choice.
\par 
\par   Turning on the RX Antenna Power via either method will prompt you a cautionay message top make sure that you really want this on. Clicking on Yes will then turn on the power while clicking no will abort.
\par 
\par 
\par See Also:
\par   }{\f5\uldb RX DC Antenna Power}{\v\f5 RX_Antenna}{\f5 
\par   }{\f5\uldb Turning Knobs}{\v\f5 Turning_Knobs}{\f5 
\par 
\par }\pard \qc {\f5 \page }{\cs16\super #{\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super #} Changing_Split}${\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super $} Changing Split Frequency}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s15 \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super K} Changing Split Frequency}} 
{\fs44 Changing the Split Frequency Knob}{\fs32 
\par }\pard 
\par   {\f5 There are 2 options for rotating the }{\f5\uldb Split Frequency}{\v\f5 Split_Frequency}{\f5  knob:
\par 
\par   Option 1: Click the left mouse button on the button that you want the knob to rotate to.
\par 
\par   Option 2: Move the mouse to the center of the knob and click either the right mouse button to rotate the knob clockwise or the left mouse button to rotate the knob counterclockwise.
\par 
\par See Also:
\par     }{\f5\uldb Split Frequency}{\v\f5 Split_Frequency}{\f5  
\par 
\par }
\par \pard \qc \page {\cs16\super #{\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super #} Changing_TX_Antenna}${\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super $} Changing TX DC Antenna Power}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s15 \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super K}
 Changing TX DC Antenna Power}} {\fs44 Changing TX DC Antenna Power}
\par \pard {\f5 
\par   There are 2 options for changing }{\f5\uldb TX DC Antenna Power}{\v\f5 TX_Antenna}{\f5 
\par 
\par 
\par   Option 1: Move the mouse cursor to the center of the knob and click either the right of left mouse button. the right mouse button rotates the knob clockwise and the left mouse button turns the knob counterclockwise.
\par 
\par   Option 2: Clicking on either button (ON or OFF). with the right mouse button will select that choice.
\par 
\par   Turning on the TX Antenna Power via either method will prompt you a cautionay message top make sure that you really want this on. Clicking on Yes will then turn on the power while clicking no will abort.
\par 
\par 
\par See Also:
\par   }{\f5\uldb Turning Knobs}{\v\f5 Turning_Knobs}{\f5 
\par   }{\f5\uldb TX DC Antenna Power}{\v\f5 TX_Antenna}{\f5 
\par 
\par }\pard \qc {\f5 \page }{\cs16\super #{\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super #} Changing_VFO_A}${\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super $} Changing VFO A}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s15 \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super K} Changing VFO A}} {\fs44 
Changing VFO A}{\fs32 
\par }\pard 
\par {\f5   There are 4 options for tuning }{\f5\uldb VFO A}{\v\f5 VFO_A}{\f5 .
\par 
\par   Option 1: Move the mouse cursor over the digit you wish to tune. While  holding down the left mouse button, move the mouse left to tune down or right to tune up. Release the left mouse button when you have finished tuning. 
\par 
\par   Option 2: Move the cursor over the digit you wish to tune . Click the right mouse button. The cursor will disappear and the select digit will be highlighted. Moving the mouse will now change this digit, right will increase & left will decrease. To exit 
from this mode, click either mouse button.
\par 
\par   Option 3: Click on the button marked }{\f5\uldb VFO A}{\v\f5 VFO_A}{\f5 . This will bring up a }{\f5\uldb Number Pad}{\v\f5 Number_Pads}{\f5  on your display.
\par 
\par   Option 4: Click on A=B. This option sets}{\f5\uldb VFO A}{\v\f5 VFO_A}{\f5  to the current frequency of }{\f5\uldb VFO B}{\v\f5 VFO_B}{\f5 .
\par 
\par See Also:
\par     }{\f5\uldb Number Pad}{\v\f5 Number_Pads}{\f5 
