\par     }{\f5\uldb VFO B}{\v\f5 VFO_B}
\par \pard \qc \page {\cs16\super #{\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super #} Changing_VFO_B}${\footnote \pard\plain \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super $} Changing_VFO_B}K{\footnote \pard\plain \s15 \f4\fs20 {\cs16\super K} Changing VFO B}} {\fs44 Changing VFO B}

\par \pard 
\par  {\f5  There are 4 options for tuning }{\f5\uldb VFO B}{\v\f5 VFO_B}{\f5 .
\par 
\par   Option 1: Move the mouse cursor over the digit you wish to tune. While  holding down the left mouse button, move the mouse left to tune down or right to tune up. Release the left mouse button when you have finished tuning. 
\par 
\par   Option 2: Move the cursor over the digit you wish to tune . Click the right mouse button. The cursor will disappear and the select digit will be highlighted. Moving the mouse will now change this digit, right will increase & left will decrease. To exit 
from this mode, click either mouse button.
\par 
\par   Option 3: Click on the button marked }{\f5\uldb VFO B}{\v\f5 VFO_B}{\f5 . This will bring up a }{\f5\uldb Number Pad}{\v\f5 Number_Pads}{\f5  on your display.
\par 
\par   Option 4: Click on B=A. This option sets }{\f5\uldb VFO B}{\v\f5 VFO_B}{\f5  to the current frequency of }{\f5\uldb VFO A}{\v\f5 VFO_A}{\f5 .
