\par \pard {\f5 
  All knobs have a fundamental method for turning them. Right clicking in the center on the knob will increase the knobs value. Left clicking in the same area will decrease it. Most knobs have additional methods of turning them which can be looked up unde
r the appropriate knob.
\par   There are 19 different knob drawings. Some knobs have more than 19 settings & as such, when the knob is increased or decreased, it may not seem to change. This is only because the two settings access the same drawing. The internal value will have moved.

